              "condition": "value === true",
              "onceOnly": true,
              "setGlobal": { "found_access_logs": true, "mole_identified": true, "database_theft_understood": true },
              "sendTimedMessage": { "delay": 2000, "message": "Root. The access logs all point the same way. Crypto Lab terminal, forty-eight hours before we deployed to Portland, the operations plan open for forty-seven minutes. And the file under root says what the four-site night was really for: our threat database. It's Nightshade. It was always Nightshade. I'm sorry. I trained with him. If anything off that box hasn't gone through the relay yet, put it through. I want the whole chain in front of him." }
